#
# Save states for the 2600 core (hdl/atari2600_core.sv describes them).
# Applied by scripts/prepare_rtl.py after atari7800_mister.patch, to the copy
# in build/upstream/; the vendored files stay untouched and keep their MIT
# notices.
#
# Every module of the console that holds registers gets three ports,
# ss_en/ss_si/ss_so, and every one of its clocked blocks ends with one line
#
#     if (ss_en) {ss_so, reg_a, reg_b, ...} <= {reg_a, reg_b, ..., ss_si};
#
# so that while ss_en is high all its registers form one shift register
# (the extra first bit is a chain stage of its own). Modules pass the chain
# through their submodules first, then through their own blocks, so the
# registers of the whole console are one chain. Arrays are listed element by
# element. The memories are not on the chain: the RIOT RAM (second port) and
# the FA2 work RAM get an ss_mem_* port that ss_hold hands over, and ss_hold
# also blocks the CPU's RIOT RAM writes.
#
# Left off the chain: cpuclk and lfsr_6_instant in TIA.sv (never
# instantiated), the ARM schemes (not built: NO_ARM_MAPPER), video_mux's
# blend frame store and the registers only blend uses (the core ties blend
# off; on the chain they would keep the 64 KB store in the bitstream), and
# the 7800 parts of top.sv. Instances in cpuclk and in top.sv's Atari7800 module
# (neither is elaborated here) leave the new ports unconnected, which lint
# reports as PINMISSING; a 7800 build would connect Atari7800's.
#
